            {
                "entry_id": "6f246a0d-547b-3dbd-930b-8cc75389ffc5",
                "word": "dameret",
                "pos": "noun",
                "lang_code": "fr",
                "forms": [
                    {
                        "form_id": "0d3345a5-ea67-40d4-9de7-01ce9e342ca1",
                        "entry_id": "6f246a0d-547b-3dbd-930b-8cc75389ffc5",
                        "tags": [
                            "plural"
                        ],
                        "form": "damerets"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "90bcc67d-6ec5-31cf-8ef5-557fd88b3a63",
                        "entry_id": "6f246a0d-547b-3dbd-930b-8cc75389ffc5",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Homme soigneux de sa parure et fort empressé de plaire aux dames."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "dated"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "c0719c06-dbcd-435c-a29f-acafcee36d91",
                                "sense_id": "90bcc67d-6ec5-31cf-8ef5-557fd88b3a63",
                                "text": "C’est vrai, tu es un dameret, toi, une vraie poule mouillée que l’on prend pour un homme."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "ee5a9aa3-b9c4-4a5d-bc5a-0e05998b30aa",
                                "sense_id": "90bcc67d-6ec5-31cf-8ef5-557fd88b3a63",
                                "text": "— Ne sont-ce pas des galants et des damerets que vous voyez chez cette femme ? N’y a-t-il pas d’autres courtisanes !"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "2f78fc61-85c9-491b-bcbc-f002aed7a80f",
                                "sense_id": "90bcc67d-6ec5-31cf-8ef5-557fd88b3a63",
                                "text": "Certes M. Béraud n’avait rien du dameret ; il inspirait à première vue un respect mêlé de crainte qui n’avait rien de commun avec la séduction."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "73e11839-0488-4122-b805-947fdba92659",
                                "sense_id": "90bcc67d-6ec5-31cf-8ef5-557fd88b3a63",
                                "text": "Ce magistrat dameret mourut jeune, laissant de sa cousine Marianne Cleenewerck, fille de l’acquéreur de Crayencour, trois fillettes dont j’ai déjà décrit la première, la petite ombre en costume de chanoinesse, une rose à la main."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "03b10585-c10e-4e75-a1bb-3750fc22c0e8",
                        "source_entry_id": "6f246a0d-547b-3dbd-930b-8cc75389ffc5",
                        "source_sense_id": "90bcc67d-6ec5-31cf-8ef5-557fd88b3a63",
                        "source_sense_description": "Homme voulant plaire aux dames",
                        "target_lang_word": "ladies' man",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "ladies' man",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "15e792db-f5f9-37a4-85d2-41931195878b",
                                        "entry_id": "88ff4da1-2068-31a7-a057-f3580dd3022e",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Alternative form of lady's man."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "alt-of",
                                            "alternative",
                                            "idiomatic"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "774f2f9e-66cd-4172-aca9-65b8c333a660",
                                                "sense_id": "15e792db-f5f9-37a4-85d2-41931195878b",
                                                "text": "[S]he told me very frankly that whenever I returned, she would leave her mate and come to me, as she preferred me above all others. I was becoming a ladies' man after a lifetime of bashfulness!"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "97b768eb-4d10-403c-818a-69e706136179",
                        "source_entry_id": "6f246a0d-547b-3dbd-930b-8cc75389ffc5",
                        "source_sense_id": "90bcc67d-6ec5-31cf-8ef5-557fd88b3a63",
                        "source_sense_description": "Homme voulant plaire aux dames",
                        "target_lang_word": "womanizer",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "womanizer",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "6ed4c222-32bb-3d26-8829-b4ebc9ea9f2d",
                                        "entry_id": "22e85a65-8c36-3384-a08e-88fe858d2f19",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A man who habitually flirts with and seduces, or attempts to seduce, women."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "607858f5-b55a-4552-b886-435584250e60",
                                                "sense_id": "6ed4c222-32bb-3d26-8829-b4ebc9ea9f2d",
                                                "text": "Getting back into the dating game after a painful divorce is never easy, and the proliferation of womanizers looking to take advantage of your vulnerability only makes things worse."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "32c9d901-64f0-4af0-933d-8db786a6bb40",
                                                "sense_id": "6ed4c222-32bb-3d26-8829-b4ebc9ea9f2d",
                                                "text": "A couple of months ago, in a piece about the language of self-involvement, I quoted a girlfriend of Woody Allen as having described the actor as “very much of a womanizer, very self-involved”."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "6c2a1058-de31-42a4-b874-d2e5d47d71f5",
                                                "sense_id": "6ed4c222-32bb-3d26-8829-b4ebc9ea9f2d",
                                                "text": "Sometimes the stereotype is framed as light and cheeky—think the “boys will be boys” mentality exemplified by sitcom womanizers such as How I Met Your Mothers Barney Stinson or '''Two and a Half Mens Charlie Harper."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    }
